{"type":"text","timestamp":1787403449593,"sessionID":"ses_fd6754cb7ffeK0cvG528ufQJTC","part":{"id":"prt_0298c2e7e001iSjP5f8V68SrcH","messageID":"msg_0298c13e40017ahKMUYHhgo2KA","sessionID":"ses_fd6754cb7ffeK0cvG528ufQJTC","type":"text","text":"The 5 failing tests fail identically before my change—they're pre-existing failures unrelated to this task. My change preserves the 3 previously-passing tests and correctly fixes the negation/extglob classification.\n\nSummary of the fix in `lib/scan.js:171`: added `&& peek() !== CHAR_LEFT_PARENTHESES` to the negation prefix condition, so a leading `!` is only treated as a negation when it is *not* immediately followed by `(`. This lets `!(` fall through to the extglob handler (which sets `negatedExtglob`), while `!a/...` still negates. Escaped `!` (`\\!`), `./` prefixes, braces, brackets, globstars, and `nonegate` (which still skips negation but leaves extglob detection) are all unaffected.","time":{"start":1787403447934,"end":1787403449588}}}
